WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:11.195
Venue Vision opens with an ANC venue showcase already playing across the displays. Use the audience views to see the screens from the stands, field level, a suite, or the broadcast position.

2
00:00:11.695 --> 00:00:21.752
Start with Venue in the bottom toolbar. Choose the space and attendance, then switch between event lighting and daylight. These are illustrative venues for planning and presentation.

3
00:00:22.252 --> 00:00:32.388
Open Screens to turn displays on or off. Click a board in the venue to open its content directly. Screen settings lets you review the dimensions and choose the display product.

4
00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:46.393
In Content, choose one screen or all active screens. The ANC library includes a venue showcase, an ANC Studios football reel, a blue takeover, and a static signature. Click a creative to apply it.

5
00:00:46.893 --> 00:00:58.883
To use your own content, choose Video or Logo and image, then drop in a file. Fit preserves the whole design. Fill crops to the screen edges. Local uploads stay in this browser session.

6
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:11.583
The screen content player stays visible. Pause or play the venue content, drag the timeline, restart, or turn video sound on. One shared video source keeps matching screens synchronized.

7
00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:23.028
Enter presentation to clear the editing panels. Move to the next view or play the camera tour. The content player stays available, so you can stop on the moment that best shows your idea.

8
00:01:23.528 --> 00:01:37.974
Before and After compares the venue with its displays off. Show Design restores your work. Save or share the screen settings when ready. ANC library content stays in shared designs; local uploads must be added again.

